WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- But last time, you and
your brothers mentioned

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.210
that you were working on new music.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:07.290
So asking for a friend, how's that going?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.150
When am I gonna get some new music?

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.480
- We're usually like
really cryptic about this.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.670
And I just kind of feel
like that's really stupid.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.523
I don't know why we do that.
- Yeah.

00:00:16.523 --> 00:00:17.970
- So we're working on new music for sure.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.636
- [Kelly] Okay.
- And I can tell you-

00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:20.469
(crowd cheers)

00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:21.626
- [Kelly] I'm excited,
I love y'alls music.

00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:23.430
- I can tell you that I think it's

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.010
my favorite stuff we've ever done.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:29.860
And it's basically

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.250
an evolution of the sound

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.900
in a way that I think
is really natural for us

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.630
and feels like a great next step.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.463
And we're working with some people

00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:38.310
we've always wanted to work with.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.778
And I can't wait for everyone to hear it.

00:00:39.778 --> 00:00:41.399
(crowd cheers)

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:46.380
- I know, I said this last
time that y'all were here

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.690
but I loved your show.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.450
Like I had never been able to
like really watch a full show.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.070
And it's so interesting cause
we would be on The Voice

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.300
and you forget.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.530
Like you're sitting next to like,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.364
I'm like oh, you're super talented.

00:00:57.364 --> 00:01:00.330
You just forget cause
you're all just hanging out.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.420
And I was at your show and
I was like, holy I know him.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.000
I was like, I was like, I was like,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.287
it was just, we can't say
that on daytime, but whatever.

00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:11.730
But I was just freaking out
because y'all were so good.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.010
It was the songs were so
good, the energy was so good.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.843
- Thanks a lot.

00:01:14.843 --> 00:01:16.110
- [Kelly] The crowd Like loved it.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.578
And I loved the fact that
the crowd was like totally

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.390
all different walks of life.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.320
Like all different time.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.880
That's my favorite kind
of crowd where you're like

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.770
nowhere would you find these people.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.727
That's my favorite kind of musical crowd.

00:01:27.727 --> 00:01:28.560
- I agree with you.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.490
- [Kelly] Cause I feel
like music can do that.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.360
Like bring randos together.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.350
- Absolutely can.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.560
And I feel like the fun thing
in this last couple years

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.600
specifically has been
that we've really seen

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.474
that distinction of,

00:01:37.474 --> 00:01:42.143
beyond the kind of OG fans
who've been there forever,

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:46.650
to a lot of the older people
who have come to our shows,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.300
perhaps watched The Voice or other things.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.310
And then younger people
who were introduced to us

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.770
in the last couple years
and think we're a new band.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.603
It's like this-

00:01:53.603 --> 00:01:54.436
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:54.436 --> 00:01:55.320
- It's like, oh yeah.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.640
- People think you're a new band?

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.500
That's my favorite thing that people do.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.730
Like if I perform
somewhere and they're like

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.260
oh my gosh, you can sing.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.943
And I'm like, well.

00:02:04.322 --> 00:02:05.970
Well a little.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.830
And I'm like, but it is
my favorite thing cause

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.810
you know that person, no,
they didn't mean offense,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.190
they just hadn't really heard anything.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.940
And I'm like, okay, well thank you.

